{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5QG9SV3NwUnHLhTazp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient wooden door stands before you, its surface weathered by centuries of wind and rain. Iron bands cross its face in patterns that might be runes, might be mere decoration. A single keyhole glows faintly — waiting.*\n\nYou present the key.\n\n*A sound like a held breath releasing. The tumblers turn — not mechanically, but organically, like bones settling into joints. The iron bands shiver. The wood grain shifts, revealing faces that were always there, always watching.*\n\n*The door swings inward.*\n\nBeyond: a corridor lit by no visible source. The air tastes of old stone and something sweeter — possibility, perhaps. Or memory. The walls breathe slowly, in and out, as if the passage itself is alive and has been sleeping.\n\n*A whisper escapes the threshold:*\n\n**\"You held the right shape. Enter, or stand forever knowing what you chose not to see.\"**\n\n*The door will not stay open long. Already the hinges are sighing, already the weight of the wood remembers its purpose is to close.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":237,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}